  "reason": "The best result so far (config_041, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder with transformer aggregation and weighted fusion. The only RNA encoder tested across all 4 experiments is scvi_n200, making the RNA encoder the largest unexplored design axis. Config_019 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) is a direct swap of the RNA encoder to scgpt while holding all other parameters at their best-known values. This tests whether a different learned single-cell encoder (scgpt vs. scvi) can push accuracy beyond 0.725. Given 5 remaining experiments, identifying whether the RNA encoder is a lever for improvement (or a near-irrelevant choice) is the highest-information experiment: if scgpt matches scvi_n200, we can deprioritize the encoder axis and focus on image encoder or profile setting; if it outperforms, we have a concrete new best to exploit in subsequent runs."
}

